TASK 01 - Study earth-api README
================================

STATUS: DONE

What we learned:

1. earth-api is a modular Earth Intelligence platform.

2. It separates the system into 5 main layers:
   - Data & Preprocessing
   - Shared Geospatial Backbone
   - Task-specific Adapters
   - Rules & Analytics
   - Orchestrator & API

3. Data preparation must be separated from analysis.

4. A shared feature extraction layer can serve multiple
   analysis tasks.

5. Not every analysis requires AI.
   Rule-based and statistical analysis are important.

6. An orchestrator is responsible for connecting the
   different processing stages.

7. FastAPI can expose the complete analysis workflow.

What GeoScanAI can reuse:

- Layered architecture
- Provider/data preparation separation
- Shared feature extraction concept
- Task-specific analysis modules
- Rules + analytics
- Central orchestration
- FastAPI service

What GeoScanAI should NOT copy directly:

- ResNet architecture
- U-Net architecture
- Deforestation-specific workflow
- Their exact folder structure
- Their exact data pipeline

Decision:

Use earth-api as an architectural reference,
not as a codebase to copy.